  "body": {
    "id": "prop:certificate-infeasibility",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Exactly one operational alternative holds: either the exact algorithm returns \\(E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star}\\), or \\(\\operatorname{Opt}_{\\mathrm{sw}}=+\\infty\\).  The latter is equivalent to\n\\[\n \\bigcup_{S\\in\\Pi}K_{\\mathrm{sw}}(S)\\ne\\Omega,\n\\]\nequivalent to rejection of every sparse switching certificate of length at most \\(B_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\), and equivalent to absence of a finite correctly typed generic acquisition on which the full unconditional procedure returns nonfailure.  The alternative is decided with at most \\(2^{|\\mathcal A|}\\) distinct oracle queries and\n\\[\n 2^{O(|\\mathcal A|+|\\mathrm{LIT}|+\\min\\{M,2^{|\\mathcal A|}\\})}\n \\operatorname{poly}(N_{\\mathrm{in}}+N_{\\mathcal O})\n\\]\nwork.  Infeasibility is relative to the operational predicate and is not a semantic nonidentification certificate.\n",
